# CQ-02 · frame-shot-inventory
#
# Question: Which camera angle × framing combinations does the corpus actually
#           use, and how many documents use each?
# Persona:  P1 — generation-pipeline engineer. The coverage question a shot
#           library asks before it trusts a value set: which of the documented
#           combinations has anything ever been written in?
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.3.3 (`vso:angle`, `vso:framing`); §2.1
# Form:     SELECT — one row per combination in use
# Note:     Neither value list is SHACL-closed in v1.x — §2.1 lists the §5.3.1 /
#           §5.3.3 value lists among the things no shape examines, and §8.2
#           forbids narrowing them mid-version. So this answer reports what the
#           corpus writes, never what a producer is allowed to write.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?angle ?framing (COUNT(DISTINCT ?doc) AS ?documents)
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?scene a vso:Composition ; vso:viewedBy ?cam .
    ?cam vso:angle ?angle ; vso:framing ?framing .
  }
}
GROUP BY ?angle ?framing
ORDER BY ?angle ?framing
